#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105573 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105715 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf98ee24-7774-5674-8a1e-63f4f6d225c0" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Reciprocal Function"}] :question/id #uuid "625c532a-d455-5b15-880d-e9fc5ae8ee72" :question/math-academy-id "e-374" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int \\left(\\dfrac 2 x\\right)\\, \\textrm{d} x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the constant factor rule and take the coefficient $2$ out of the integral. Then we compute the integral of $\\dfrac 1 x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\frac{2}{x})\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2ln⁡|x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105574 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105716 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c865ec2-5bed-5892-966b-a586097be923" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating the Sum of a Reciprocal Function and a Power Function"}] :question/id #uuid "9c57c69e-efa2-5e82-992c-53570e61af09" :question/math-academy-id "e-375" :question/problem "Find the integral of $\\dfrac 1 {2x} + 3x$ with respect to $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\frac{1}{2x}+3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int 3x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+3\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}ln⁡|x|+3\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{1+1}}{1+1}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{ln⁡|x|}{2}+\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105575 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105720 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "df7dddc6-a4fd-5b1b-9b73-8528e5224ca9" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Reciprocal Function and Simplifying the Arbitrary Constant Using the Laws of Logarithms"}] :question/id #uuid "bf47e35e-da86-5f88-b1e7-0cc731c37b31" :question/math-academy-id "e-376" :question/problem "What is the antiderivative of $\\dfrac {3+2x} {x} ?$" :question/worked-solution "We separate the integrand into the sum of two fractions so that we can simplify each term. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3+2x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{3}{x}+\\frac{2x}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{3}{x}+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3ln⁡|x|+2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, let's rewrite the constant so that we can combine it with the natural logarithm. For any constant $C,$ we can always write $C =3 \\ln K$ where $K$ is some other constant. Doing this allows us to combine the constant with $3\\ln|x|$ term, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3+2x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3ln⁡|x|+2x+C \\\\  & =3ln⁡|x|+2x+3ln⁡K \\\\  & =3ln⁡(K|x|)+2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238029 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105716 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c865ec2-5bed-5892-966b-a586097be923" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating the Sum of a Reciprocal Function and a Power Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4abe304b-eb2b-5d95-b662-98795ce766a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{3/2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236297} {:answer/id #uuid "6d00a003-0364-5b3a-b73d-cf2606acaf82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{5/2}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236506} {:answer/id #uuid "b7b12b3f-b8dd-53cd-a79b-4f8d64e6c135" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}{x}^{5/2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236984} {:answer/id #uuid "c71fc3c7-fa6d-5f20-8988-65604e335a7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{3/2}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237078} {:answer/id #uuid "ca4ffb28-67bb-5e22-a3dc-17c627b249f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{5/2}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237101}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7b12b3f-b8dd-53cd-a79b-4f8d64e6c135" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}{x}^{5/2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236984} :answer-field/id #uuid "67ce5cc2-6611-553c-af07-6c3510863b9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237573}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1a6388af-23c9-54c5-98cc-a8fb2fcf5235" :question/math-academy-id "q-103593" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int ({x}^{3/2}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1})\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the sum rule and get\n\n$$\n\\int ({x}^{3/2}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1})\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {x}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nNow, using the power rule in the first term, and taking out the coefficient in the second term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{3/2+1}}{\\frac{3}{2}+1}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}{x}^{5/2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106280 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105716 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c865ec2-5bed-5892-966b-a586097be923" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating the Sum of a Reciprocal Function and a Power Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8140037d-2d2c-5542-a0ba-9edf6b7bbf28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\ln \\mid x \\mid - \\frac{2}{x} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103829} {:answer/id #uuid "0405b19e-98fb-5a56-97e4-d2d44340c6ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln \\mid x \\mid - x^{1/2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103830} {:answer/id #uuid "14506e14-75d8-5464-ba2e-4e8d416dcb89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x - 2x^{1/2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103831} {:answer/id #uuid "3737381e-42d1-5ec5-a0be-6e2c2c114442" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\ln \\mid x \\mid - 2x^{1/2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103832} {:answer/id #uuid "72930a31-c1dd-529c-95f0-0c9ed79b8c26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln \\mid x \\mid + 2x^{1/2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103833}] :answer-field/id #uuid "f13e7011-de56-51ec-9c85-6d23ec9e1c7c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103828}] :question/id #uuid "60e355f2-c5a8-565b-92ee-4e1844ef9c98" :question/math-academy-id "q-29857" :question/problem "Find the integral of $\\frac{2}{x} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}$ with respect to $x$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339052 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105715 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf98ee24-7774-5674-8a1e-63f4f6d225c0" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Reciprocal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f88c79e-e25c-5fcd-a473-3f9adb3d4e9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{7}ln⁡|x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336327} {:answer/id #uuid "58b493c2-73d3-5db1-af15-0200a2937632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{ln⁡|x|}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336844} {:answer/id #uuid "daf20704-2d65-5753-af90-f6e026c52e12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{7}ln⁡|x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337940} {:answer/id #uuid "ec4261ce-b5b3-5551-9fbd-56937e1eea24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{\\sqrt{7}}ln⁡|x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338091} {:answer/id #uuid "f7a97ce9-ff10-5758-b496-1ffe87d0bb3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-ln⁡|\\sqrt{7}x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338202}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f88c79e-e25c-5fcd-a473-3f9adb3d4e9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{7}ln⁡|x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336327} :answer-field/id #uuid "f930863c-55bb-55cc-bd9d-51b8ae4abea3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338715}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d9daecf1-e255-5c0c-a433-fdc798f551aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-72059" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the constant factor rule and take the coefficient $-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}}=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}}\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{7}}=-\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{7}$ out of the integral. Then we compute the integral of $\\frac{1}{x},$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}}\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{7}ln⁡|x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
